  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Traxillagenin may interact with HuT78 through a series of molecular targets. Specifically, Traxillagenin is linked to T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3, which is a target of Phyllofolactones F, and both of these are targets of Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)-, which in turn targets HuT78. Additionally, Traxillagenin is also associated with M059J, which targets HuT78. These findings indicate that Traxillagenin may exert its biological effects through multiple pathways, ultimately leading to interactions with HuT78. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where Traxillagenin acts as a modulator of signaling pathways involving CD3 and other proteins, potentially influencing cellular processes in HuT78. The strength of the evidence is moderate, as the scores are relatively close, but the exact nature of the interaction remains uncertain without further experimental validation.",
